cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Aether-Lang: a Rust runtime for topological machine learning"
abstract: >-
  A Rust workspace for a small language runtime, a bounded topological
  computation core, ML primitives, and a sparse-event kernel prototype.
  Topology is used as a systems signal: embeddings, residuals, binary
  streams, and scheduler state are converted into geometric or topological
  objects, then used for execution, diagnostics, convergence checks, or
  pruning. Includes a Lean 4 verified kernel.
